ada:defaultMonitoredProperties.description:
The monitored properties this procedure defines by default — the ROWS of the table. An entry is a bare string or a schema:DefinedTerm naming the property, or a ROW OBJECT keyed by the schema:valueName of the columns above, which is what carries the mapping:

  {"monitoredProperty": "⁸⁴Sr", "targetSpecies": "Sr", "collector": "L2"}

targetSpecies is OPTIONAL and its absence is meaningful, not missing data. A procedure routinely monitors masses that determine no target species -- interference monitors, gas background monitors -- and those rows are orphans by design: ⁸³Kr, ¹⁶⁷Er²⁺ and ¹⁷³Yb²⁺ in the Zhang 2022 Rb-Sr procedure are monitored and corrected for, never determined.
